// Protocol between the controller and the app (phone / PC).
//
// UART frame (Libs/usart), passed unchanged between BLE and UART by the nRF52:
//
//   | 0xA5 | CMD | SEQ | LEN_L | LEN_H | PAYLOAD | CRC_L | CRC_H |
//
//   CMD     — Command below. A reply has the request's CMD with bit 0x80 set
//             (START_SESSION 0x01 -> 0x81). A request that fails gets ERROR (0xFF).
//   SEQ     — chosen by the app, copied to the reply (pairs replies with requests)
//   PAYLOAD — the command's protobuf model: <Name>Request in the request,
//             <Name>Response in the reply. An empty model encodes to 0 bytes.
//
// Compatibility rules:
//   - never reuse or renumber a command or a field, remove it and mark it `reserved`
//   - value 0 of every enum means "not set"
//   - breaking changes bump ProtocolVersionMajor (app_protocol.h)
//   - every change bumps the version (flaps_protocol.h) and is listed in proto/CHANGELOG.md
//
// The protocol is split by who uses it:
//   flaps_common.proto   — session, device info, commands, statuses (both apps, bootloader)
//   flaps_state.proto    — state, telemetry, events, manual control (both apps)
//   flaps_logic.proto    — logics (both apps)
//   flaps_firmware.proto — firmware update, reboot (both apps, bootloader)
//   flaps_user.proto     — logics without the rest of the configuration (user app)
//   flaps.proto          — configuration, CAN sniffing, dev mode (technician app only)
// A user app session (StartSessionRequest.app_id = AppIdUser) gets ERROR(UNKNOWN_COMMAND)
// for the technician's commands and no LOG / AMP_OUT / CAN_SNIFF frames.

